RainBIOS firmware for Javascript 1983
=====================================

These redistributable ROM images provide RainBIOS MSX1 firmware, the native and
browser-edition Omega MSX2 default, and the browser edition's Philips NMS 8250
profile:

  rainbios_msx1.rom           MSX1 main BIOS, 32 KiB
  rainbios_msx2.rom           MSX2 main BIOS, 32 KiB
  rainbios_msx2_sub.rom       MSX2 Sub-ROM, 16 KiB
  rainbios_disk.rom           Generic WD2793 disk ROM, 16 KiB
  rainbios_omega.rom          Omega unified EEPROM image, 512 KiB
  rainbios_nms8250_disk.rom   Philips WD2793 disk ROM, 16 KiB

They were built from RainBIOS commit
abb1a34df3830fa0771b4a4bd35889207c812b6d:

  https://github.com/salvogendut/rainbios

Rebuild and import the exact Omega firmware from a clean sibling checkout of
that revision with:

  make import-rainbios-roms

For a checkout elsewhere, use:

  make import-rainbios-roms RAINBIOS_DIR=/path/to/rainbios

The script invokes the RainBIOS MSX1 and MSX2 main, Sub-ROM, generic disk-ROM,
and NMS8250 disk-ROM targets, cooks the unified Omega image, verifies every
digest, and only then replaces the bundled copies.
RainBIOS documents the required assembler, compiler, Python, and companion
BBC BASIC checkout in its own README.

The unified image follows the Omega EEPROM layout: each 256 KiB jumper bank
contains four consecutive 64 KiB images for slot 0 and slot 3 subslots 0, 1,
and 3. RainBIOS is placed in slot 0, its Sub-ROM in 3-0, and the WD2793 disk
ROM in page 1 of 3-3. Both halves contain the same redistributable recipe, so
either emulated JP1 bank boots identically. See:

  https://msxmakers.design.blog/proyectos/proyectos-msx/omega-home-computer/omega-paso-a-paso/cocinando-la-rom-del-omega/

